<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8"/>
<meta content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" name="viewport"/>
<meta content="dark" name="color-scheme"/>
<meta name="theme-color" content="#05070d"/>
<title>Starsilk Compendium</title>
<meta name="description" content="Starsilk Compendium — the Starsilk canon dossier: principal and peripheral character folios, the Drakken register, WorldsVault, and supporting lore material, plus faceted discovery, an entity index, a relationship observatory, a canon inspector, curated tours, and chronology."/>
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}"/>
<meta property="og:type" content="website"/>
<meta property="og:site_name" content="Starsilk Compendium"/>
<meta property="og:title" content="Starsilk Compendium"/>
<meta property="og:description" content="Principal and peripheral character dossiers, the Drakken register, canon chronology, and WorldsVault reference material, plus discovery, entities, relationships, canon, and tours."/>
<meta property="og:url" content="{{ canonical_url }}"/>
{% if og_image_url %}<meta property="og:image" content="{{ og_image_url }}"/>
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/>{% else %}<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary"/>{% endif %}
<meta name="twitter:title" content="Starsilk Compendium"/>
<meta name="twitter:description" content="Principal and peripheral character dossiers, the Drakken register, canon chronology, and WorldsVault reference material, plus discovery, entities, relationships, canon, and tours."/>
<link rel="manifest" href="manifest.webmanifest"/>
<style>
{{ style_css }}
/* Preserve the HTML hidden contract even when component CSS sets display. */
[hidden]{display:none!important}
</style>
</head>
<body data-museum-shell="unified">
<a href="#mainContent" class="skip-link" tabindex="0">Skip to dossier content</a>

<video id="brandkit-watermark" muted playsinline aria-hidden="true"></video>
<aside class="index" id="index"><div class="index-head"><b>Starsilk / Index</b><button aria-label="Toggle dossier navigation" id="menuToggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="indexPanel">Index</button></div><div class="index-panel" id="indexPanel"><div class="index-panel-inner"><nav>{% for group in nav_groups %}<details class="nav-group" open><summary>{{ group.label }}<span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="nav-group-body">{% for item in group.links %}<a href="#{{ item.id }}">{{ item.label }}</a>{% endfor %}</div></details>{% endfor %}</nav><small>Web Edition · Character pages are print-separated.</small></div></div></aside>
<main id="mainContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="page-controls"><button type="button" id="expandAllBtn">Expand all</button><button type="button" id="collapseAllBtn">Collapse all</button><button type="button" id="sidebarToggle" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="index">Hide index</button><button type="button" id="modeToggle" aria-pressed="false" hidden>Archive tools</button><button type="button" id="copyImplementationPrompt" hidden>Copy implementation prompt</button><span id="copyPromptStatus" class="visually-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span><div class="page-controls-search"><label for="dossierSearch" class="visually-hidden">Search dossier titles and content</label><input type="search" id="dossierSearch" placeholder="Search dossier&#8230;" aria-label="Search dossier titles and content" autocomplete="off"/><span id="dossierSearchStatus" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div></div>
{% for section in sections %}{{ section.render() }}
{% if section.id == 'cover' %}<div class="museum-entrance" data-museum-shell="unified">
<section class="museum-hero" aria-labelledby="museum-hero-heading">
<div class="museum-hero-inner">
<div class="eyebrow">Unified Compendium</div>
<h1 id="museum-hero-heading" class="museum-hero-title">One Compendium.<br/>Nine ways in.</h1>
<p class="museum-hero-lede">Source-backed exploration surfaces stand alongside the complete dossier below, all reading from the same authored canon. Nothing here is invented for the interface — unknowns stay unknown.</p>
<div class="museum-hero-actions">
<a class="museum-cta primary" href="#mainContent">Enter the Compendium</a>
<a class="museum-cta" href="discover/">Start discovering</a>
</div>
<dl class="museum-hero-stats" aria-label="Collection totals">
<div><dt>Compendium records</dt><dd>{{ museum_stats.record_count }}</dd></div>
<div><dt>Published media objects</dt><dd>{{ museum_stats.object_count }}</dd></div>
<div><dt>Cross-referenced links</dt><dd>MUSEUM_LINK_COUNT_PLACEHOLDER</dd></div>
<div><dt>Chronology events</dt><dd>{{ museum_stats.event_count }}</dd></div>
<div><dt>Curated tours</dt><dd>{{ museum_stats.tour_count }}</dd></div>
<div><dt>Machine-enforced canon locks</dt><dd>{{ museum_stats.canon_lock_count }}</dd></div>
</dl>
</div>
</section>

<section class="museum-modules" aria-labelledby="museum-modules-heading">
<h2 id="museum-modules-heading" class="visually-hidden">Explore the Compendium</h2>
<div class="museum-module-grid">
<a class="museum-module" href="discover/"><span class="museum-module-eyebrow">Discover</span><h3>Faceted discovery</h3><p>Search and filter every stable record with source-backed excerpts and AI context packets.</p></a>
<a class="museum-module" href="entities/"><span class="museum-module-eyebrow">Entities</span><h3>Entity index</h3><p>Stable, shareable permalinks for every principal, peripheral, and Drakken record.</p></a>
<a class="museum-module" href="objects/"><span class="museum-module-eyebrow">Objects</span><h3>Published media</h3><p>Browse the published media collection with provenance, without loading the archive.</p></a>
<a class="museum-module" href="relationships/"><span class="museum-module-eyebrow">Relationships</span><h3>Relationship Observatory</h3><p>Directional evidence of what the Compendium actually cross-references — nothing more.</p></a>
<a class="museum-module" href="canon/"><span class="museum-module-eyebrow">Canon</span><h3>Canon Inspector</h3><p>Machine-enforced validation locks protecting selected established facts.</p></a>
<a class="museum-module" href="tours/"><span class="museum-module-eyebrow">Tours</span><h3>Tours &amp; local library</h3><p>Curated stable-ID routes, plus a private browser-local bookmarks and collections shelf.</p></a>
<a class="museum-module" href="chronology/"><span class="museum-module-eyebrow">Chronology</span><h3>Interactive chronology</h3><p>Only direct authored markers and durations appear here — unknowns stay explicit.</p></a>
<a class="museum-module" href="worldsvault/"><span class="museum-module-eyebrow">WorldsVault</span><h3>Cosmic topology</h3><p>A source-backed topology explorer for direct authored cosmic relations.</p></a>
</div>
</section>

<section class="museum-data-strip" aria-labelledby="museum-data-heading">
<div><div class="eyebrow">Data &amp; AI</div><h2 id="museum-data-heading">Machine-readable publication</h2><p>Agent-oriented documentation and deterministic machine derivatives for the whole collection.</p></div>
<div class="museum-data-links"><a href="agents/AGENT_GUIDE.md">Agent guide</a><a href="machine/index.json">Machine index</a><a href="llms.txt">llms.txt</a><a href="sitemap.xml">Sitemap</a></div>
</section>

<section class="museum-compendium-lead" aria-labelledby="museum-compendium-heading">
<div class="eyebrow">Full Compendium</div>
<h2 id="museum-compendium-heading">The complete dossier continues below</h2>
<p>Everything that follows is the original Starsilk Compendium in full: principal and peripheral folios, the Drakken register, WorldsVault reference prose, the canon ledger, and supporting material — unabridged.</p>
</section>
</div>{% endif %}
{% endfor %}<section class="page footer" data-folio="{{ footer_folio }}"><div class="eyebrow">Standalone reference</div><h2>Keep the contradiction.<br/>Keep the silhouette.</h2><p>This is the Web Edition: canon prose lives in this document, media is delivered as externalized, deduplicated files under <code>assets/media/</code> rather than embedded inline. Character locks override stale sheet annotations, unresolved canon conflicts remain explicit, and no third-party network resource is required to read the dossier.</p><p class="subtle" style="font-size:.78rem">Text, art, and media in this dossier are shared here for reference within the Starsilk project. Their presence on GitHub is not a grant of reuse rights &#8212; see <a href="RIGHTS.md">RIGHTS.md</a>.</p></section>
</main>
<script>
{{ app_js }}
</script>
<script src="offline-client.js"></script>
</body></html>
